117. Note. If a man has done evil, let him not do it again and again;
let him not take pleasure in it, for the accumulation of evil is sorrow.

118. If a man has done good, let him do it again and again; let him

119. take pleasure in it, for the accumulation of good is joy. The wicked man sees good as long as his evil deed has not matured;

120. but when the evil deed matures, then he sees evils. The good man
sees evil as long as his good deed has not matured, but when

121. the good matures, then he sees good things. Let no one think little of
evil (thinking): "it will not come to me"; by the falling of a drop
the water-jar is filled, the fool is filled with evil, gathering it little by little.

122. Let no one think little of good (thinking): "it will not come to me";
by the falling of a drop the water-jar is filled, the wise man is filled

123. with good, gathering it little by little. A merchant, as if avoiding a dangerous
road, with a small band of companions, being very wealthy, [would avoid it]...
